Read CLAUDE.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, and MIGRATION.md in full at the start of every session and obey every rule in them — the invariants, security rules, money discipline, node protection, and conventions. CLAUDE.md is the single source of truth for how we work; ARCHITECTURE.md and MIGRATION.md define system structure and portability. For what the product must do, read docs/aafnai/DECISION_REGISTER.md — it is the current product authority, and where it and any other document disagree, it wins — then docs/aafnai/PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md and the relevant spec in docs/specs/.

Emit Founder Checkpoints per CLAUDE.md (Session protocols → Founder Checkpoints) after each meaningful unit of work — three lines, no walls of text. Update TASKS.md whenever a task is completed. Append a detailed entry to DEVLOG.md (see CLAUDE.md journal rules) after every meaningful change.

**Hard stops.** Do not touch anything that moves money, or any table holding grief data or health data, unless the prompt explicitly authorizes it. Stop and ask.

The actual protected tables, verified against supabase/migrations:
- Grief data: **shraddha_dates** (deceased_name, relation, gotra, tithi fields) and **ceremonies**.
- Health data: **progress_photos**, **measurements**, **bodyweight_logs**, **workout_logs**, **set_logs**.
- Also protected wherever it appears: **bookings.intake_response**, which currently holds grief data for pandit bookings and injury disclosures for fitness bookings. It is a known invariant-2 defect, not a normal column — see ARCHITECTURE.md §4.
- Contractor data: **providers.payout_reference** and the **payout_ledger** / **payments** tables.

Never write code that auto-sends a ritual date without a recorded human confirmation — that is invariant #1 and it has no exceptions.

**Money math ships with tests.** Any change to pricing, commission splits, take rates, refunds, or proration ships with a test in the same commit.

Commission is **20% on recurring coaching and 20% on one-off consultations** (`docs/aafnai/DECISION_REGISTER.md` §L, TY-COMM-01). **Commission is rounded first and the coach takes the exact remainder** — rounding the coach's share first gives a different answer on odd amounts (TY-COMM-02). The worked fixtures, already implemented in `web/src/lib/money/split.test.ts`:

- USD 100.00 → coach 80.00, commission 20.00
- A coach-discounted 600.00 package at 540.00 → coach 432.00, commission 108.00
- A platform-funded 10.00 promotion on a 100.00 service → customer pays 90.00, coach still 80.00, platform net 10.00
- Refund 25.00 of a 100.00 service → coach reversal 20.00, commission reversal 5.00
- USD 10.01 at 20% → commission 2.00, coach 8.01
- A 510.00 six-month term → 85.00 per service month at 68.00 / 17.00, 425.00 undelivered after one month

The superseded Aafnai-era figures ($70/$30, $12/$8, $59.50/$25.50) are historical. They are preserved as `commission.coaching.v1` and `.v2` in `web/src/lib/policy/registry.ts` so old ledger rows stay explicable — never as the rate for anything new.

**No rate, price, or payout schedule may be written anywhere but `web/src/lib/policy/`.** A percentage typed into a component or a migration is how a marketing page and the ledger quietly drift apart.

Any migration adding or changing tables or RLS policies ships with an RLS test in the same commit. **The test runner exists:** `npm test` in `web/` uses Node's built-in runner with no added dependency; `npm run verify` runs typecheck, lint and tests together.

**Copy and tone convention** (defined here; CLAUDE.md has no tone section): nav items, buttons, and section labels use Title Case. No emoji anywhere in the product. No exclamation marks, urgency mechanics, countdowns, or scarcity language anywhere in the pandit vertical. Ritual terminology is used correctly or not at all; if unsure of a term, ask rather than guess. In fitness, never characterise a weight increase or decrease as automatically good or bad, and never nag or use streaks — daily weighing is a capability, not an obligation.

Treat a command that produces no output/progress for its defined idle window as hung: do not wait on it or retry-loop — follow CLAUDE.md's Interruption & failure protocol ("HANGS"). Never busy-wait or poll in a shell loop. Hang-prone commands (seed, RLS tests, db:reset, db:push, backup) must run through `scripts/lib/with-idle-timeout.mjs`, which kills a child only after a no-output window and prints why; never wrap the dev server. Elapsed time alone is never the kill signal; preserve diagnostic output before any kill.

Commit messages must read as a professional human developer's commits: conventional style (feat:, fix:, chore:, refactor:), concise, factual. Never mention AI, agents, models, or tooling in any commit message, code comment, or file.

Before the final commit of any session, follow the end-of-work documentation protocol in CLAUDE.md: propose updates to ARCHITECTURE.md, MIGRATION.md, README.md, or the records in docs/aafnai/; wait for approval; then commit work plus approved doc changes only. Then give the founder explanation, then append one entry to CTO-BRIEF.md per CLAUDE.md (Session protocols → CTO Briefing).
